<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13333" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēscensus</span></b> ,
			ūs, m.
		descendo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a descent</i> (rare; not in Cic. and Caes.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qua illi descensus erat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall. C. 57, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Concr., <i>a descending way, a descent</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">difficilis et praeruptus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hirt. B. G. 8, 40, 4</span></i>
			 and 5; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facilis descensus Averno,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 126</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ipso descensu Jovis speluncae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					16, 26, 46, § 110</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Luc. 19, 37</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic. (acc. to descendo, <i>no.</i> I.
			B. 5), obscene, <i>a lying down</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 2, 5, 13</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
